RW-075 architecture/boundary delta review, round 1 (Nabu)
Date: 2026-09-06. Lane: forge handoff nabu (bounded, read-only delta).

VERDICT: FAIL — confidence high.

Findings:

- BLOCKER — admission is self-mintable and does not prevent profile
  broadening. `AdmissionReceipt` is publicly constructible, while public
  `admit_package` accepts any digest and `approve_package` hardcodes the
  bootstrap-profile digest for any `EXTENDED_V1` package
  (`crates/sley-vm/src/exec_package.rs:227-240,679-744`; exports at
  `crates/sley-vm/src/lib.rs:22-26`). The claimed negative test only
  cross-binds a float package to another package's approval; it never
  attempts approving that float package itself
  (`crates/sley-vm/tests/rw075_exec_closure.rs:728-757`). This does not
  encode the separately accepted authority promised by
  `docs/spec/EXEC_PACKAGE_V1.md:74-84`.
- BLOCKER — the 64 MiB package-envelope ceiling is not enforced.
  `EXEC_PACKAGE_MAX_BYTES` is defined but unused; `package_digests`
  checks the image and individual sections only, while the dependency
  section has no total/count ceiling
  (`crates/sley-vm/src/exec_package.rs:83-99,555-620,633-670`). A package
  can exceed the contract's total envelope bound.
- BLOCKER — the separate R2 exit gate exists but can false-pass. It runs
  the record-only checker, which explicitly never reads implementation
  sources, and omits the production marker checker
  (`scripts/check_r2_exit.py:121-135`;
  `scripts/check_exec_package_v1.py:4-7`). Review acceptance is an
  unanchored substring search for `"PASS"`, so a FAIL review mentioning
  PASS can satisfy the gate (`scripts/check_r2_exit.py:144-165`).
- PASS — inner image topology remains unchanged. No delta exists in
  `lower.rs`, `host_abi.rs`, VM-extended conformance, or the SLEYBC02
  specification; the new path feeds package image bytes through the
  existing loader and preserves the callee table
  (`crates/sley-vm/src/execute.rs:631-681`).
- PASS — raw hashing is narrow and not yet profile-wired. It exposes one
  bounded BLAKE3 variant and documents RW-080 as the future import-wiring
  point (`crates/sley-vm/src/raw_hash.rs:63-74,105-147`;
  `docs/spec/RAW_HASH_V1.md:3-6`).
- PASS — RW-080 is materially concrete and remains contract-only. It
  explicitly states no graph/C1 exists, specifies module
  interfaces/dependencies, construction provenance, C0 limits, and
  anti-copy evidence
  (`machineresearch/sley-2.0/reweave/rw-080-contract.md:3-10,14-140,155-216`).

Validation performed by reviewer: reviewed working-tree delta against
